{
  "description": "Shared conformance vectors of the bridge's encoding C, protocol 1 (plan section 2c, \"The messages\"). The C# and TypeScript tests read this file. 'canonical': each encoder writes exactly 'wire' from 'message', and each decoder reads 'wire' back to 'message'. 'decode': valid messages in other forms that decoders must read as 'message'. 'malformed': messages decoders must refuse, with the id a refusal may be addressed to (null when none can be trusted). In 'message', 'payload' is the text after the TAB.",
